  '/research/compare':
    'Built 2026-09-23 against Research Compare.dc.html at Rev 2026-09-23.24, on the design\u2019s option (b) for the three inputs this data plan does not carry and on the Owner\u2019s answer to where the rows come from. WHERE THE ROWS COME FROM (Owner 2026-09-23): the prototype\u2019s view reads \u201cfrom Symbol verdict\u201d, and verdicts here are prose claims with no stance, level or horizon, so the view is typed on the page (stance \u00b7 floor \u00b7 ceiling \u00b7 days, on the address) and says so beside it. The structures are the active rules in Trade \u203a Rules whose dimensions match the stance \u2014 sell vol reads short_vol, bullish and bearish read direction, buy vol reads long_vol \u2014 so on DEV a sell-vol view gives five of the six (bear call, bull put, CSP, covered call 10% OTM, iron condor). The prototype\u2019s calendar and 1\u00d72 ratio are not rules here and do not appear; a rule with no placement is a row that says why. Until the reader types levels, floor and ceiling are \u00b110% of spot and an amber note says they are nobody\u2019s view. PLACEMENT, stated under the table: a short put at the highest listed strike at or below the floor, a short call at the lowest at or above the ceiling, a spread\u2019s wing about 5% beyond its short (the rule\u2019s legs carry no wing rule), a covered call by its own otm_pct, a bull call spread long at the money. Expiry is the first listed at least the horizon out, a monthly when the rule\u2019s time dimension says monthly. MEASURED (DEV 2026-09-23, PLTR): the plugin\u2019s end-of-day chain for 16 OCT answers 122 contracts with one untraded; spot is the session\u2019s close from the same day as the chain; the research route /research/option-expirations answers 404, so expiries are read from the plugin\u2019s own catalogue (new fetchChainExpirations). BUILT, per Rev .24\u2019s table: legs in the design\u2019s own line (STO 172.5P \u00b7 16 OCT @ 2.36), net, backing, \u0394 \u00b7 vega \u00b7 \u03b8, the payoff overlay, \u2192 Plan (to Plans narrowed to the name, the same door Option screen\u2019s \uff0b Plan is \u2014 Plans takes no contract), and How big with the backing cap as room to the 85% gate \u00f7 one unit\u2019s backing, read from the same exposure hook Risk \u203a Sizing cites. HALF-BUILT: the conviction cap is Playbook stats\u2019 own size-cap rule (full \u00b7 half under the sample floor \u00b7 none under profit factor 1.2) applied to the strategy service\u2019s record by structure and taken as a share of the backing cap; the label is written out in full (Cash Secured Put \u00b7 by structure: 19 closed, 95%) with regime split owed in grey, and never the prototype\u2019s \u201cIV rank > 65\u201d. OWED, IN PLACE: the tail cap bar reads \u201ctail cap \u00b7 needs the 20-day distribution \u2014 not computed\u201d and every size carries \u201c2 of 3 caps\u201d \u2014 on DEV that is the whole point, because without the tail cap the backing room sizes a bull put spread at two hundred units, and a missing cap only ever makes a size too large; POP \u00b7 EV 20d \u00b7 p10 are \u2014 with the reason on the header; Can you get filled is the EmptyState in the design\u2019s exact words plus its optional liquidity line per structure (the thinnest leg\u2019s OI and volume, \u201ca liquidity proxy, not a spread\u201d); \u2212 fills and EV net are \u2014, and the page\u2019s header line reads \u201cEV net of fills \u00b7 owed (quotes)\u201d. The payoff band (20-day p10\u2013p90) is not drawn and the caption says so. EXTRACTED BEFORE DUPLICATING (\u00a714.2): the size-cap rule moved from Playbook stats to utils/sizeCap.ts with a record-shaped input, since Compare is its second reader (the prototype\u2019s own words: \u201cfeeds the conviction cap on Compare\u201d); parseOptionTicker joined buildOptionTicker as its inverse; positionGreek, daysTo and winRateBand are reused as they were. DIVERGED, EACH WITH ITS REASON. The Margin column is Backing: the gate this page divides is Backing & Model\u2019s pool, which charges a short put its strike and a spread its width, not the broker\u2019s Reg T margin, and dividing a backing room by a margin figure would mix units. Premiums are the session\u2019s last trade (day_close), not a mid, because the plan carries no quote, and every place a premium appears says so. Swatch colours are the identity tokens (contract \u00b7 strategy \u00b7 instance) and amber, not the prototype\u2019s literals. The \u201ctrade-off, in words\u201d panel writes each structure\u2019s sentence from its numbers rather than the prototype\u2019s hand-written prose, and a structure sized to none says which cap refused it. DOORS OPENED: Option screen\u2019s \u21c4 Compare, drawn disabled until today, now opens this page with that contract\u2019s strike as the floor (checked by its href; DEV\u2019s screener has no contract row to click); Risk \u203a Sizing\u2019s sentence no longer says Compare is unbuilt, and says instead that Compare hands on a Plan rather than a sized candidate; Signal Decay\u2019s comment says Compare reads conviction off the structure\u2019s record, not a lens\u2019s decay \u2014 its visible sentence was already true. Swept: the ticker, four \u2192 Plan links and Playbook stats; a row click toggles its curve (aria-pressed); the stepper steps from the previous value (five clicks, five steps \u2014 a first version stepped once); over-cap turns the size red and the binding cell amber; bearish leaves only the bear call spread; a typed floor rewrites the address and re-places the puts. Checked at desktop and 1024: no page overflow, the fifteen-column table scrolls in its own container.'
